 "function": "cloudgen.texture.regime_weights",
 "doc": "Scalar-like (0-d) inputs at the point where the raw total exceeds 1 (-34.75 deg, back-traced to -39.75): the outputs are 0-d and normalized to sum to exactly 1 (the `scale` division). Float64 closed form: 1e-9. Outputs closed/open/street are the function result; convective (climate.convective_tendency of the latitude in degrees), cold (the cold-air ramp smoothstep(0, 8, |back lat| - |lat|) in degrees) and total_raw (closed + open + street before the normalization, which divides by it where it exceeds 1) are intermediates, there to localize a mismatch; they share the tolerance. params.constants holds the knees and weights written in the code. Output `closed`, `open`, `street`, `convective`, `cold`, `total_raw` is 0-d: shape [] in case.json, one item of data.bin.",
